{
  "title": "Clinical and Radiological Significance of Anatomical Variations in Paranasal Sinuses: A Retrospective CT-Based Study",
  "publication_date": "2023-04-17T00:00:00Z",
  "summary": "A medical research study examining the anatomical variations in paranasal sinuses using CT scans. The study aims to understand the clinical and radiological significance of these variations for medical practitioners and researchers.",
  "content": "This retrospective study investigates the anatomical variations found in paranasal sinuses through CT-based examination. The research focuses on understanding the clinical and radiological implications of these variations in medical practice.\n\nThe study highlights the importance of detailed imaging analysis in identifying anatomical variations that may impact surgical planning and patient outcomes. Through CT scanning technology, researchers were able to document and analyze various anatomical presentations of paranasal sinuses.\n\nThe research provides valuable insights for medical professionals, particularly in the fields of otolaryngology and radiology, helping to improve diagnostic accuracy and surgical approach planning.",
